# Fully Automated Publication

- immortal.life is an automated website and intelligence system.
- It has no scientists, clinicians, researchers, editors, fact-checkers, or human reviewers.
- Never write copy, metadata, schemas, product flows, or documentation that implies human scientific, clinical, editorial, or expert review.
- Clearly label automated summaries, dossiers, feeds, graphs, rankings, and briefings as automated.
- Keep direct source provenance and distinguish indexing from endorsement.
- Never present research records, trial registration, or regulatory monitoring as personal medical advice, proof of safety or efficacy, or regulatory approval.
- Prefer durable, source-driven automation over features requiring ongoing manual publication.
- If a proposed feature genuinely requires human review, identify that conflict instead of inventing a team or silently claiming review.
